---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL } from '../data/site';

const description =
  'How GamersXpress handles data: visit statistics through Google Analytics, no accounts, no personal data.';

const lastUpdated = new Date('2026-11-12');
const lastUpdatedDisplay = lastUpdated.toLocaleDateString('en-US', {
  year: 'numeric',
  month: 'long',
  day: 'numeric',
  timeZone: 'UTC',
});
const lastUpdatedIso = lastUpdated.toISOString().slice(0, 10);
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy | GamersXpress"
  description={description}
  breadcrumbs={[
    { name: 'GamersXpress', path: '/' },
    { name: 'Privacy', path: '/privacy' },
  ]}
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-10">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-tight">Privacy</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-ink-muted">
      GamersXpress is a static website. This page explains what the site
      collects and what it does not.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-ink-subtle">
      Last updated <time datetime={lastUpdatedIso}>{lastUpdatedDisplay}</time>
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-8 text-xl font-bold tracking-tight">What the site collects</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-ink-muted">
      Anonymous, aggregate visit statistics: which pages are read and how
      people arrive at the site, summed up across visitors rather than tracked
      per person. The site has no accounts, no comment system, and no forms
      that store what you send it. We do not ask for or keep personal data
      through the website.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-8 text-xl font-bold tracking-tight">Analytics</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-ink-muted">
      The site uses Google Analytics 4 (measurement ID G-NC7DCQ7KT1) to count visits
      and see which pages are read. Google receives the visit and processes it
      under its own privacy policy. The numbers it reports are aggregate.
      Google's script is loaded from Google's servers on every visit, so
      before you choose, Google may receive a signal that a page was viewed,
      with technical details such as your IP address and browser. It stores
      no analytics cookies on your device until you accept.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-8 text-xl font-bold tracking-tight">Cookies</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-ink-muted">
      You choose. On your first visit a banner asks whether Google Analytics
      may set its cookies (names beginning with _ga). Until you accept, it
      sets none. Rejecting keeps them off, and nothing else changes on the
      site. Your choice is saved on your device in local browser storage, not
      as a cookie. You can change it at any time with "Cookie settings" in
      the footer. The site sets no cookies of its own. If advertising cookies
      are ever added, this page will be updated before they are enabled, and
      the date above will change.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-8 text-xl font-bold tracking-tight">Fonts and pictures</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-ink-muted">
      The fonts and the pictures on this site are served from gamersxpress.com
      itself. Your browser does not contact Google or any other font service
      when you read a page. Where an article picture comes from another
      source, such as a game's Steam store page or Wikimedia Commons, we keep
      our own copy and credit it under the picture with a link to where it
      came from. Your browser only contacts that source if you follow the
      link.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-8 text-xl font-bold tracking-tight">Third-party links</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-ink-muted">
      Articles link to sources, game stores, and other sites. When you follow
      a link you leave gamersxpress.com, and whatever that site does is up to
      that site.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-8 text-xl font-bold tracking-tight">Questions</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-ink-muted">
      If you have a question about this page, email
      <a
        href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}
        class="text-accent underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-accent-hover"
      >
        {CONTACT_EMAIL}
      </a>. If you email us, we receive your address and message as normal
      email — that is separate from anything the website itself collects. See
      also the <a
        href="/contact"
        class="text-accent underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-accent-hover"
        >contact page</a
      >.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
